      <summary>What is WLCSP?<span class="sc-faq-mk">+</span></summary>
      <div class="sc-faq-a">Wafer-level chip-scale packaging completes the package at wafer level before singulation. The finished part is essentially the die with its bump array, ready for direct board attachment.</div>
    </details>
      <details class="sc-faq">
      <summary>What does Hana's WLCSP flow include?<span class="sc-faq-mk">+</span></summary>
      <div class="sc-faq-a">The flow includes incoming inspection, back-grind and dicing, die-attach film, flip-chip and WLCSP attachment down to 80 µm Cu pillar bump pitch, wafer-level test, singulation and tape-and-reel packing.</div>
    </details>
      <details class="sc-faq">
      <summary>Does Hana do wafer bumping or RDL?<span class="sc-faq-mk">+</span></summary>
      <div class="sc-faq-a">No. Bumping and redistribution-layer processing remain with the foundry or bumping house. Hana takes over from incoming wafer inspection through back-grind, dicing, die-attach film, flip-chip and WLCSP attachment, wafer-level test and packing.</div>
    </details>
      <details class="sc-faq">
      <summary>When is WLCSP the right choice?<span class="sc-faq-mk">+</span></summary>
      <div class="sc-faq-a">WLCSP is suited to products where package footprint and profile are important, including mobile, wearable and other space-constrained applications.</div>
    </details>
      <details class="sc-faq">
      <summary>How is WLP controlled?<span class="sc-faq-mk">+</span></summary>
      <div class="sc-faq-a">Processing takes place in cleanroom, ESD-controlled areas, with assembly qualified on first articles and per-unit traceability maintained through the flow.</div>
    </details>
    </div>
